WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.120
Nic Cage, Sonic's triumphant return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.280
and a gay take on Jane Austen.&nbsp;
It's been a crazy year for comedy.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.640
You have probably already heard of one of the&nbsp;
most talked-about movies of the year, Everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.840
Everywhere All at Once. This is a movie that&nbsp;
defies definition by dipping its hotdog-shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:25.280
fingers into several different genres, such as&nbsp;
action, adventure, drama, sci-fi, martial arts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.560
and many more. One of the constants throughout the&nbsp;
mind-bending experience of watching this film is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.600
just how funny it is, but that doesn't mean you&nbsp;
won't need some help understanding the ending.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.120
Everything Everywhere All at&nbsp;
Once is an absurd dramedy about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.800
a Chinese-American immigrant named Evelyn who&nbsp;
is thrust into a maddening multiversal story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.680
revolving around her family. This is one of&nbsp;
those movies that manages to balance the bonkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.400
randomness of its humor with the grounded&nbsp;
and realistic portrayals of its characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.520
to amazing effect, thanks in no small&nbsp;
part to the performances of its main cast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.640
Upon release, the movie was met with universal&nbsp;
acclaim and praise for its creative premise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.320
powerful performances, and genuinely hilarious&nbsp;
comedy. It has gone on to be described by many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.880
as one of the best films ever made, and&nbsp;
it really can only be seen to be believed.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.760
On the complete opposite end of the&nbsp;
comedy spectrum is Jackass Forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:25.760
a movie that has no pretensions of grandeur. The&nbsp;
Jackass franchise has existed for over two decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.920
simply by giving us hilarious movies of funny guys&nbsp;
and gals hurting themselves on camera. Sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.040
that's all you need. And considering that one of&nbsp;
the stunts in this movie involving a bull nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.760
killed star Johnny Knoxville, these guys literally&nbsp;
put their blood, sweat, and tears into making it.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.480
Jackass Forever is the fourth mainline&nbsp;
film in the series, and like the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.320
it focuses on putting its stars in dangerously&nbsp;
compromising situations through extreme stunts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.680
pranks, and general tomfoolery. This latest&nbsp;
installment features almost all the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.200
cast members from previous films and also&nbsp;
aims to pass the torch of self-endangerment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.080
to a new generation of daredevils. With&nbsp;
even more on-set injuries than ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.040
there's a reason that Jackass Forever has become&nbsp;
the most highly-rated film in the franchise.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.880
It should come as no surprise to film buffs out&nbsp;
there that a Pixar movie ended up on this list.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.520
Pixar films tend to strike a balance between&nbsp;
humorous and heartwarming while wrapped in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.400
high-concept package, and Turning Red&nbsp;
is no exception. This film features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.440
an incredible cast and ambitious script that&nbsp;
has sparked some unfortunate internet drama.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.720
Turning Red is one of the latest films from&nbsp;
Pixar Studios, telling the story of Mei Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.720
a 13-year-old Chinese-Canadian girl who magically&nbsp;
gets turned into a giant red panda during moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.320
of intense emotion. The film portrays this&nbsp;
transformation as both serious and comedic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.240
with it being a condition passed down through&nbsp;
her family that is meant to be controlled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.880
Once Mei and her friends realize the unique&nbsp;
potential of using the panda to their advantage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.360
they fully embrace using it for&nbsp;
money-making clout to hilarious results.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.880
"I'm paying for the red panda. Not this garbage!"

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.280
As a classic coming-of-age tale about a&nbsp;
teenage girl going through major changes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.080
the story walks the line between goofy&nbsp;
jokes and more serious family drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.080
to create a film that many regard&nbsp;
as one of Pixar's best in years.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.280
One of the more strange and humorously named&nbsp;
movies on this list is The Unbearable Weight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.520
of Massive Talent, which stars and&nbsp;
is entirely focused on Nic Cage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.480
who plays a version of himself. The film is&nbsp;
an action-comedy that follows the escapades of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.160
Cage as he deals with a struggling film career as&nbsp;
well as family issues. All these things and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:47.600
come to a head as the famed actor gets himself&nbsp;
involved in a massive plot beyond his control.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.880
As a self-indulgent but undeniably charming&nbsp;
film, The Unbearable Weight of Massive Talent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.320
shows a Nic Cage whose career is struggling amid&nbsp;
numerous box office flops and who is taunted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.400
visions of his past self. Out of desperation, Cage&nbsp;
is brought to Spain to meet with a wealthy fanboy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.640
From there the plot goes off the rails, involving&nbsp;
drug trafficking, kidnapping, and the CIA. By&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.760
being appropriately tongue-in-cheek, this movie&nbsp;
has been regarded by many as one of Cage's best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:21.280
roles in decades while also managing to be a&nbsp;
genuinely hilarious comedy at the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.200
Could this be the start of a Nic Cage&nbsp;
renaissance? That remains to be seen.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.680
As one of the most anticipated&nbsp;
animated comedies of the year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:35.120
it should come as no surprise to fans that The&nbsp;
Bob's Burgers Movie lived up to the expectations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.240
Based on the award-winning Fox series of the same&nbsp;
name, this movie took everything fun about Bob's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.000
Burgers and turned it up for the big screen. Bob's&nbsp;
Burgers is about the Belcher family with Bob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.840
Linda, Tina, Gene, and Louise all dealing with&nbsp;
the difficulties of running a burger business.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:56.560
The show has gone on for 12 seasons&nbsp;
since 2011 and has gained a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:02.080
cult following for its wacky humor, puns,&nbsp;
musical numbers, and endearing characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.480
It was only a matter of time before Bob's&nbsp;
Burgers got a feature film of its own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:12.160
The Bob's Burgers Movie focuses on the Belchers&nbsp;
suffering financial woes after being denied an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.800
extension on their business loan as well as&nbsp;
having a massive sinkhole form right in front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.280
of their restaurant. Upon release, critics&nbsp;
have agreed that The Bob's Burgers Movie has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:26.800
a successful mixture of laugh-out-loud silliness&nbsp;
while maintaining a satisfyingly heartfelt story.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.920
When people think of not-terrible video game&nbsp;
movies, one of the few that comes to mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.960
is probably Sonic the Hedgehog. The first&nbsp;
film was released in 2020, with audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.360
everywhere being pleasantly surprised by&nbsp;
the portrayal of Sonic and Jim Carrey's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.000
over-the-top performance as the villainous&nbsp;
Dr. Robotnik. It is because of that success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.040
that Paramount Pictures continued the gravy&nbsp;
train with this year's Sonic the Hedgehog 2.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:56.160
"Hello, hedgehog. Did you miss me?"

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.240
Picking up where the first film left off, Sonic&nbsp;
the Hedgehog 2 begins almost eight months later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.200
as Dr. Robotnik seeks revenge against Sonic&nbsp;
with the help of Knuckles the Echidna.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.920
Sonic recruits the help of his friend Miles&nbsp;
"Tails" Prower to find the Master Emerald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:18.000
before his enemies do and save the universe as we&nbsp;
know it. This may sound like heavy subject matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.800
but Sonic the Hedgehog 2 manages to be a&nbsp;
lighthearted cartoonish adventure with lots of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:28.480
slapstick humor and tongue-in-cheek jokes along&nbsp;
the way. With a stacked cast of acting talent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:34.320
it is no surprise this film gained significant&nbsp;
buzz as being even better than the first film.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.040
The Man from Toronto is a high-octane&nbsp;
action-comedy film starring Kevin Hart, Woody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:44.640
Harrelson, and Kaley Cuoco to name a few. The Man&nbsp;
from Toronto has enough laughs and shootouts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:50.080
satisfy fans of the genre while also sporting&nbsp;
enjoyable performances from its lead actors.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:56.160
Hart stars as an unsuccessful fitness instructor&nbsp;
who desperately wants to find success selling his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.920
idea of "no-contact boxing." Over the course of&nbsp;
the story, Teddy is swept into a plot of mistaken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.600
identity when he is confused as being "The Man&nbsp;
from Toronto," a highly trained killer who is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:12.080
actually Harrelson's character. Together&nbsp;
the two go on a globe-trotting adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:18.080
while running away from other assassins and FBI&nbsp;
agents as they navigate this absurd situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.640
While the film has mostly been panned by&nbsp;
critics and audiences alike, there is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:28.080
enough comedic gold between Hart and Harrelson in&nbsp;
The Man from Toronto to keep anyone entertained.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:34.080
The recently released Chip 'n Dale: Rescue&nbsp;
Rangers implements CGI, 2D animation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:39.600
and live-action performances together in the same&nbsp;
movie. This film focuses on Chip and Dale, two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.920
cartoon chipmunks who had a popular real-life show&nbsp;
in the 1990s and have since become losers. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.960
world of Chip 'n Dale: Rescue Rangers, animated&nbsp;
characters and humans all live together and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.880
interact with each other like normal. This movie&nbsp;
seeks to blend comedy, action, adventure, mystery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:02.080
and nostalgia into a movie with lots of jokes&nbsp;
that may go over the heads of younger audiences.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.520
The story is centered around&nbsp;
the kidnapping of Monterey Jack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:10.320
another character from the original show, and&nbsp;
the investigation Chip and Dale must undertake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.320
to discover what happened to their friend.&nbsp;
For many, the main appeal of this movie is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:19.360
the countless number of cameo appearances&nbsp;
by other characters from animation history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.920
One of the more talked about appearances&nbsp;
is that of "Ugly Sonic," voiced by popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:29.760
comedian Tim Robinson as the older, uglier&nbsp;
version of CGI Sonic from Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.040
Another entry in the popular genre of movies&nbsp;
about humans becoming friends with dogs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:41.600
Dog is a road comedy about a U.S. Army Ranger with&nbsp;
PTSD given the assignment of taking a military dog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:47.120
to his friend's funeral across the country.&nbsp;
Rooted in serious topics like war, trauma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.680
family, and death is also the comedic&nbsp;
narrative of Jackson Briggs learning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.560
develop a relationship with a chaotic dog&nbsp;
that wants to destroy everything in sight.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:00.240
As with most road comedies, Briggs&nbsp;
and Lulu the dog endure several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.240
strange encounters throughout the film&nbsp;
that lead to absolute belly laughs.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.640
"You're just a demon! You're just a demon!!"

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:11.120
Dog satisfied audiences and critics&nbsp;
alike with positive reviews and made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.560
significant box office returns on its meager&nbsp;
15 million dollar budget. For dog lovers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.800
Channing Tatum lovers alike, Dog is a film&nbsp;
that has a little something for everyone.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.480
The Bad Guys is an animated comedy centered around&nbsp;
a team of criminal animals who make a living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:31.520
planning heists that fit within the reputation&nbsp;
of their species. Based on a book for children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:35.280
this film features an impressive&nbsp;
cast of actors in various roles.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.200
As a team of criminals known as The Bad&nbsp;
Guys, the animals embrace the negative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:45.120
stereotypes of their various species by plotting&nbsp;
elaborate heists led by the charming Mr. Wolf.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:48.960
Once they accidentally get pictured doing&nbsp;
a good deed during one of their schemes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:53.280
the team is roped into trying to reform&nbsp;
themselves as good guys in order to atone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:58.320
for their crimes. The Bad Guys is filled with&nbsp;
witty humor, interesting animation, and lots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.200
of exciting action that serves to make this one&nbsp;
of the higher-rated animated movies of the year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.640
More than anything, many seem to agree that the&nbsp;
film is genuinely funny for both kids and adults.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.080
It's time to talk about the Minions. With the&nbsp;
recent release of Minions: The Rise of Gru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.400
the world has once again been graced with the&nbsp;
big-screen presence of everyone's favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.840
little yellow banana-loving troublemakers. As the&nbsp;
latest in the Despicable Me and Minions franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.040
this film serves as a sequel to the first&nbsp;
standalone Minions film while also simultaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:34.080
being a prequel to the first Despicable Me&nbsp;
feature. Illumination Entertainment has managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:40.000
create some of the most iconic animated characters&nbsp;
of all time, and the film was a financial smash.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:45.520
The Rise of Gru takes place in 1975 and serves&nbsp;
to explain how the Minions came to serve the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:50.640
villainous Gru, who is only a kid at this time.&nbsp;
Gru and the minions are roped into a conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:55.680
between the Villainous 6 and their former leader&nbsp;
named Wild Knuckles as they struggle to collect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:01.120
the Zodiac Stone. Minions: The Rise of Gru is full&nbsp;
of the kind of minion-based shenanigans that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:07.600
series has become known for, with lots of yelling,&nbsp;
cartoon violence, laughing, and banana enjoyment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:12.640
This film also sparked some real-life comedy when&nbsp;
thousands of moviegoers around the world made it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:17.680
a meme to see the movie dressed to the nines&nbsp;
in suits, calling themselves "gentle minions."

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:22.480
Fire Island is a delightful romantic&nbsp;
comedy about a group of gay men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.960
vacationing on Fire Island off the coast&nbsp;
of Long Island, while the story is inspired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:31.920
by Pride and Prejudice. Things get more&nbsp;
complicated as the men navigate romances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.040
rivalries, judgment, and outrageous&nbsp;
circumstances during their weeklong stay.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.600
"And this is why straight people hate us."

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:44.640
The narrative is mainly focused on Noah as&nbsp;
he heads to Fire Island with his friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:50.080
as part of a yearly tradition among the five of&nbsp;
them. From there, Noah has to deal with various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:54.880
flames and sexual encounters as he and his&nbsp;
other friends try to have a good time while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:59.440
understanding this is the last opportunity they'll&nbsp;
get to return to the island the way they used to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:04.960
Throughout the film are humorous moments of levity&nbsp;
that embrace awkwardness and misunderstandings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:08.320
Fire Island has done considerably&nbsp;
well with the critics, with many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:18.160
praising its representation of&nbsp;
gay men and engaging characters.

